Arduino Radar System 💡

This project demonstrates a Radar System built using an Arduino Uno, an ultrasonic distance sensor, and a servo motor. The radar visuals are generated using the Processing application.

Features ✨

🔄 Real-Time Scanning: Continuously scans the surrounding area and detects obstacles.

📊 Graphical Representation: Displays radar data graphically using the Processing app.

🛠️ Interactive Components: Utilizes an ultrasonic sensor for distance measurement and a servo motor for rotation.

🛢 Compact Design: Simple and portable setup, ideal for hobbyists and beginners.

Technologies Used 🛠️

Microcontroller: Arduino Uno

Sensor: Ultrasonic Distance Sensor (HC-SR04)

Motor: Servo Motor (SG90 or similar)

Software:

Arduino IDE for coding and uploading sketches

Processing IDE for visualizing radar data


Installation and Setup 🚀

Requirements:

Arduino Uno

Ultrasonic Distance Sensor (HC-SR04)

Servo Motor

Jumper Wires

Breadboard

Processing IDE (for visualization)

Steps:

Hardware Setup:

Connect the ultrasonic sensor and servo motor to the Arduino as per the circuit diagram.

Ensure all connections are secure.

Upload Arduino Code:

Open the Arduino IDE and upload the provided sketch.

Run Processing App:

Open the Processing IDE and load the provided sketch.

Run the program to start visualizing the radar data.


